            <ArticleTitle>[Painful legs and moving toes. Neuropathy caused by cytarabine].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>869-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new case of painful legs and moving toes syndrome is reported in a patient with a neuropathy due to high-doses of cytosine arabinoside (Ara C). A few cases of this complication have been reported. The neuropathy was sensory, axonal, and incompletely regressive. Carbamazepine had a dramatic effect on pain and involuntary movements.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
